{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 46, :comments ["<b>Set your heart to all the words with which I testify among you.</b> This is not the language of testimony but the language of warning, in the manner of (Exodus 19:21) ״רד העד בעם״, and likewise (ibid.) ״כי אתה העדות בנו״. And Moshe warns here that a person should set all his thought upon the Torah, and this is why it says לבבכם — 'your heart' — and did not say שימו לבבם, so that they may serve the Holy One, blessed be He, with both inclinations, with the good inclination and with the evil inclination; and so the Sages, of blessed memory, expounded: ״I created the evil inclination; I created for it the Torah as a spice.״"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:53:34.190133627Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}